#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186151964 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ea76b57b-3289-524a-b0e3-0439e22c1f34" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Limit Using the Limit Definition of Euler's Number"}] :question/id #uuid "58b7adfb-2b39-5c37-8334-b2c24b701881" :question/math-academy-id "e-9357" :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle{\\lim_{n \\to \\infty} \\left(1+\\dfrac{1}{n}\\right)^{3n}}$." :question/worked-solution "Recall the following special limit:\n\n$$\ne = \\lim_{n \\to \\infty} \\left(1+\\dfrac{1}{n}\\right)^{n}\n$$\n\nNow, we rewrite the given limit using the algebra of limits, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\lim_{n \\to \\infty}(1 + \\frac{1}{n})^{3n} &= \\lim_{n \\to \\infty}[(1 + \\frac{1}{n})^{n}]^{3} \\\\\n&= [\\lim_{n \\to \\infty}(1 + \\frac{1}{n})^{n}]^{3} \\\\\n&= e^{3}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186151965 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "16ad6bbc-b8c4-52f6-9f24-0d8494d83b94" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Limit Definition of the Exponential Function"}] :question/id #uuid "50565e0b-0853-563f-82c7-0e6a868e5364" :question/math-academy-id "e-9358" :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle{\\lim_{n \\to \\infty} \\left(1+\\dfrac{x}{n}\\right)^{-n/2}}$." :question/worked-solution "Recall the following special limit:\n\n$$\ne^x = \\lim_{n \\to \\infty} \\left(1+\\dfrac{x}{n}\\right)^{n}\n$$\n\nNow, we rewrite the given limit using the algebra of limits, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\lim_{n \\to \\infty}(1 + \\frac{x}{n})^{-n/2} &= \\lim_{n \\to \\infty}[(1 + \\frac{x}{n})^{n}]^{-1/2} \\\\\n&= [\\lim_{n \\to \\infty}(1 + \\frac{x}{n})^{n}]^{-1/2} \\\\\n&= (e^{x})^{-1/2} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{\\frac{1}{e^{x}}}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186151966 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "31c3dfc6-edf9-5b4a-96f6-17090b07c732" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Limit Using the Limit Definition of Euler's Number: Limits Containing Variables"}] :question/id #uuid "8f06ca5f-071d-5ee4-a856-256d07887c25" :question/math-academy-id "e-9361" :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle{\\lim_{n \\to \\infty} \\left(1+\\dfrac{1}{n}\\right)^{nx/3}}$." :question/worked-solution "Recall the following special limit:\n\n$$\ne = \\lim_{n \\to \\infty} \\left(1+\\dfrac{1}{n}\\right)^{n}\n$$\n\nNow, we rewrite the given limit using the algebra of limits, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\lim_{n \\to \\infty}(1 + \\frac{1}{n})^{nx/3} &= \\lim_{n \\to \\infty}[(1 + \\frac{1}{n})^{n}]^{x/3} \\\\\n&= [\\lim_{n \\to \\infty}(1 + \\frac{1}{n})^{n}]^{x/3} \\\\\n&= e^{x/3} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt[3]{e^{x}}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
